00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:02,997
a deterministic final
answer we'll end with.

288
00:12:02,997 --> 00:12:04,580
Yeah, so the question,
is there a risk

289
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:07,680
that we get to the right answer,
but we take suboptimal steps?

290
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,180
There is.

291
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:10,420
And I'm going to be talking
about that in this lecture

292
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:10,920
actually.

293
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,020
Yeah.

294
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:15,340
So that's a basic reasoning
MDP or a language.

295
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:17,820
MDP, you can pose for
studying reasoning problems

296
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,903
in this particular setting,
and at least something

297
00:12:19,903 --> 00:12:23,220
that I'm going to be sticking
