298
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:25,820
So we'll start with
studying some classical RL

299
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,960
methods for reasoning.

300
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,460
And what I'm going
to do here is I'm

301
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:31,557
going to cover one of my
papers from NeurIPS 2024

302
00:12:31,557 --> 00:12:32,640
that you see on the slide.

