346
00:14:23,010 --> 00:14:26,970
tuning, which trains on many
correct solutions for a given

347
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:27,970
answer.

348
00:14:27,970 --> 00:14:33,102
So I'm going to write
this method out here,

349
00:14:33,102 --> 00:14:34,310
and that'll be clear for you.

350
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:36,727
So what you're going to do is
you're going to take a model

351
00:14:36,727 --> 00:14:38,570
pi of y given x.

352
00:14:38,570 --> 00:14:41,550
We'll take a question
x from my data set.

353
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:44,910
So this is my
question or problem.

354
00:14:44,910 --> 00:14:46,410
So this is my initial state.

355
00:14:46,410 --> 00:14:47,850
This is my solution
which consists

356
00:14:47,850 --> 00:14:49,250
of a sequence of actions.

357
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,970
What I'm going to do now is I'm
going to take these questions

358
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:57,690
and sample multiple solutions
from my particular model,

359
00:14:57,690 --> 00:14:59,530
from my current model
that I want to train

360
00:14:59,530 --> 00:15:00,655
in this particular setting.

361
00:15:00,655 --> 00:15:01,970
So I have a model pi theta.

362
00:15:01,970 --> 00:15:04,930
I'm going to sample multiple
solutions conditioned

363
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:10,830
on the question, given
this particular model.

364
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:14,240
So this is my model I'm
training, the initial model.

365
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,770

366
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:18,050
This is the data set.

367
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:20,210
I'm going to sample
multiple solution traces.

368
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:24,530
What I'm going to do now is
I'm going to take these traces,

369
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:26,510
evaluate the rewards
on each of them.

370
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:35,290
So I'm going to evaluate
r of Y1, r of Y2, r of Yn.

371
00:15:35,290 --> 00:15:36,190
Why can I do this?

372
00:15:36,190 --> 00:15:38,290
Because I have this
question in my data set

373
00:15:38,290 --> 00:15:41,320
which means I have a
ground truth answer,

374
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:45,600
y star, for this question
in my data set as well.

375
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:50,545
Ground truth answer
for x question.

376
00:15:50,545 --> 00:15:51,920
And what I can do
is I can simply

377
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:55,840
match whether multiple traces
or multiple trajectories

378
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:59,240
sampled from my policy pi theta
end up in the right answer

379
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:04,280
or not by checking whether the
final number was correct or not.

380
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:06,560
So what I'm doing here is
I'm taking my initial model,

381
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,960
sampling a bunch of
traces, or rolling it out

382
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:11,280
in my environment, which is
simply producing solutions

383
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:13,280
from this model
for each question

384
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:17,280
and evaluating the rewards
against the ground truth answer.

385
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:21,880
Now, what I do is I take
this particular set of Y1

386
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:25,600
to Yn's I produced, and I
retain only those ones which

387
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,720
ended up in the right answer.

388
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:34,080
So I take the set s of
Y1 to Yn, and I filter

389
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:38,500
it to get some filtered set.

390
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:41,080
Let's call it's s
tilde, which consists

391
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:49,120
of Ys, so Yj, such
that the reward is 1,

392
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:52,720
meaning these solutions
ended up at the right answer.

393
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,660
Does this procedure
make sense to people?

394
00:16:55,660 --> 00:16:56,160
OK.

395
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,760
And what I'm going
to do now is now

396
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,920
I have a bunch of traces
or a bunch of trajectories

397
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,587
that ended up at the
right answer, which

398
00:17:02,587 --> 00:17:03,760
means they're successful.

399
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:07,079
So what I can do is I can simply
try to train my model pi theta

400
00:17:07,079 --> 00:17:09,079
to imitate these trajectories.

401
00:17:09,079 --> 00:17:13,140
So I can train pi theta
to imitate S tilde.

402
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:16,040
So I'm just going to
write it down here again.

403
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:23,880
So my algorithm looks like
this for iteration 1 to some t

404
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:26,940
that I can choose
however I want.

405
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:35,080
So step one is sample Y1
to n from pi theta of dot

406
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:35,910
given x question.

407
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:38,800

408
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:43,480
The second step is
filter and generate

409
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:53,000
s tilde, which consists
of correct Y's only.

410
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:58,623
And the third step is, do
imitation or do BC or SFP,

411
00:17:58,623 --> 00:18:00,540
depending upon whatever
terminology you like--

412
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,680
you can call that--

413
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:03,340
on s tilde.

414
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:05,760
So you're training
the model now by theta

415
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,920
to produce only the
Y's that were correct.

416
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:12,160
So that's this
particular approach.

417
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:15,120
So this approach
is what is called

418
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:17,580
