599
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:25,560
So what happens is on-policy
imitation learning ends

600
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:28,880
up hurting generalization
if you do too much of it.

601
00:25:28,880 --> 00:25:30,560
And to show a result
for it, I'm going

602
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:35,080
to show you a plot here,
which is showing the test

603
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,960
performance, so the same plot.

604
00:25:36,960 --> 00:25:41,000
But now the x-axis is the
number of correct answers

605
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:43,720
you get in this filtered
set that I was describing

606
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,740
to you earlier per question.

607
00:25:45,740 --> 00:25:49,660
So you can scale it up for
how much ever you want.

608
00:25:49,660 --> 00:25:52,280
The size of s tilde multiplied
by a constant factor

609
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:53,960
is shown on the
x-axis, and we're

610
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:57,260
plotting the performance of the
resulting RFP trained model.

611
00:25:57,260 --> 00:25:58,760
The interesting
thing to notice here

612
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:01,180
is that, initially,
your error goes down.

613
00:26:01,180 --> 00:26:02,597
So as you do more
and more correct

614
00:26:02,597 --> 00:26:04,513
solution traces, as you
generate more and more

615
00:26:04,513 --> 00:26:05,900
of these correct
solution traces,

616
00:26:05,900 --> 00:26:08,060
your error goes down,
as you see initially.

617
00:26:08,060 --> 00:26:09,600
But then beyond a
point, your error

618
00:26:09,600 --> 00:26:11,940
starts to go up in this
particular setting.

619
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:13,973
So you find that,
beyond a point,

620
00:26:13,973 --> 00:26:15,140
you get diminishing returns.

621
00:26:15,140 --> 00:26:16,515
And there's no
way you can simply

622
00:26:16,515 --> 00:26:18,600
generate more solutions
from your policy,

623
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:20,460
mimic them, and get
better performance.

624
00:26:20,460 --> 00:26:23,043
And in fact, the error even goes
up on some of these data sets

625
00:26:23,043 --> 00:26:25,240
that you see up here.

626
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:27,470
[INAUDIBLE]

627
00:26:27,470 --> 00:26:28,590

628
00:26:28,590 --> 00:26:30,710
You can think of it as S--

629
00:26:30,710 --> 00:26:31,730
the size of S tilde.

630
00:26:31,730 --> 00:26:33,230
It's the number of
correct solutions

631
00:26:33,230 --> 00:26:34,710
you retain per question.

632
00:26:34,710 --> 00:26:36,530
So the question was,
what is the x-axis?

633
00:26:36,530 --> 00:26:38,270
The x-axis is number of S tilde.

634
00:26:38,270 --> 00:26:39,580
For each S.

635
00:26:39,580 --> 00:26:44,590
So the plot it's basically,
S tilde times 8K in the plot

636
00:26:44,590 --> 00:26:47,450
because that's the number of
prompts that you see up here.

